 -- Thomas Lamprecht <thomas@lamprecht.org>  Fri, 26 Jun 2026 15:38:08 +0200

pi-coding-agent (0.79.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of the Pi coding agent as the "pi" command.
  * Ship the compiled application plus its pruned production dependency
    closure under /usr/lib/pi and run it through a thin /usr/bin/pi launcher,
    so the package stays self-contained apart from the Node.js runtime.
  * Pin undici to the latest Node.js 20-compatible release (7.x) in the bundled
    closure. Upstream pins undici 8.x, which raises the runtime floor to
    Node.js 22.19; the 7.x line keeps the same API surface the agent uses and
    drops the floor to Node.js 20.18.1, so the package runs on the Node.js that
    Debian ships.
  * Compile the committed model snapshot instead of running pi-ai's code
    generation, which fetches live model catalogs over the network (and runs
    .ts files directly, requiring Node.js >= 22.6). This keeps the build
    reproducible and buildable on Debian's Node.js 20.

 -- Thomas Lamprecht <thomas@lamprecht.org>  Sat, 20 Jun 2026 16:22:15 +0200
